dsh-two-stage-promotion
=======================

Derived from @linxin666/dsh-liangshen (Apache-2.0,
https://github.com/zhu1090093659/dsh-web), which is in turn derived from
xiaobright/dsh-anchored-standard (MIT,
https://github.com/xiaobright/dsh-anchored-standard).

This package renames the two-phase preset to 二阶段晋升模式
(two-stage-promotion), keeps the host-side preset sync mechanism, and adds a
feature-detected Session API shim so the preset plugin runs on both the legacy
DSH (`session.events`) and the current DSH (`session.snapshotEvents()`,
0.1.2-rc.1 and later) without an engines floor above 0.1.2-alpha.4.

Local fixes carried from the liangshen debug session (2026-09-04):
- tool-bootstrap.mjs: `session.events` -> feature-detected
  `session.events` / `session.snapshotEvents()` (the legacy read crashed every
  turn on the current DSH with "Cannot read properties of undefined
  (reading 'length')").
- Black-box diagnostics: listener crashes append full stacks to
  /tmp/two-stage-promotion-crash.log; a MOUNT marker is written per apply().

